		(property "Note" "Crystal drive-limit resistor in series with U3 OSC2, 0 ohm fitted. Size it at bring-up: measure Y1's amplitude at OSC1 with a <= 1 pF probe, compute drive ~ ESR * (pi * f * Vpp * (C0 + CL))^2 / 2, and fit Rs (typically ~X_C2, a few hundred ohms) if it exceeds ~100 uW. CX3225SA allows 200 uW max; a rail-to-rail 40 MHz Pierce can reach 0.2-0.5 mW. Rs eats start-up margin (~4.5x at gm min with 0 ohm), so fit only what the measurement asks for."
			(at 0 0 180)
			(unlocked yes)
			(layer "F.Fab")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "a029a04c-fbec-4c01-8393-518acccafc2c")
