		(property "Quote" "Rev 2.1: not yet quoted. DigiKey 9698138, in stock (operator, 2026-10-12)."
			(at 0 0 270)
			(unlocked yes)
			(layer "F.Fab")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "43ab263d-8263-41be-944c-a8f762a01ca8")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 0.8 0.8)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "U3 time reference, 40.000 MHz fundamental crystal, the 13.5.6 fallback design (operator, 2026-10-12: easy to source). CX3225SA40000D0PTWCC (datasheets/cx3225sa_e.pdf): 40000 kHz; D0 = CL 8.0 pF; P = +/-50 ppm at 25 C; T = -40..150 C; W = +/-200 ppm over temperature, ~20x inside the MCP2518FD's +/-0.5 %; ESR <= 50 ohm; C0 <= 3 pF; drive 10 uW typ, 200 uW MAX (see R43); AEC-Q200. Pads #1/#3 are the crystal and #2/#4 ground, matching Crystal_GND24. Start-up margin |R_neg| ~ gm/(w^2 C1 C2) with C1 = C2 ~ 12 pF (8.2 pF + ~4 pF stray): 224-336 ohm vs 50 ohm ESR = ~4.5-6.7x. Rev 2.0's ABLS2 at CL 18 pF had 0.8-1.3x. Check Kyocera's recommended land (1.45 x 1.05 mm pads) against the KiCad 3225 footprint at layout. The MPN's last two letters 'CC' are an individual specification (the catalogue standard is 'HH'): the catalogue ESR/C0/drive figures are confirmed for this exact part by DigiKey's listing (8 pF, 50 ohm) only; confirm C0 and drive with Kyocera or at bring-up. ROTATION: a 90-degree error puts the crystal on the GND pads and shorts OSC1/OSC2 through the lid - pin-1 on the assembly drawing."
			(at 0 0 270)
			(unlocked yes)
			(layer "F.Fab")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "d655cc30-973c-4e59-9185-db43ea6df00d")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 0.8 0.8)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
			)
		)
